This type of action is only possible because most Canadians get their
legal knowledge from American TV, and they don't understand their 
rights or the limits on police powers.

In Canada, you can not be taken down to the station for questioning 
unless you agree to go. The police can do nothing if you refuse, 
unless they lay a charge and arrest you.

Similarly, police can not examine computer files without a 
warrant if you refuse permission, and there is nothing they can do if
you refuse. To obtain a warrant, they have to have probable cause.

The same applies to computer systems. If they hassle you, take them to 
small claims court.

