You can only make this argument stick against a.b.p.e.  Not against what
occurs in alt.sex.  Both were banned.  And anyway, I seriously doubt that
a.b.p.e was banned because of copyright issues.  If it was, then great:
the university is upholding valuable intellectual property rights.  But if
it wasn't, then we need to get to the bottom of it before something less
controversial is banned also.  The copyright issue is just one of many
that has been dug up after the fact to try and justify the newsgroups'
removal.

> Yes, and the straw-man extreme case is always the one bandied around.

The no-sex faction also use extreme cases: "pornography causes sex crimes".
Both camps are guilty of using straw men.

We need to get to the bottom of this and find out exactly why these newsgroups
were banned.  Not the after-the-fact justifications, but the original reason
that caused the powers that be to get their back up and direct kre to remove
them.  Maybe the reason was a good one, or maybe it was an ill-considered
reaction based on faulty information, media hype, or the fear of lawyers.
Hiding behind "costs" and "copyrights" won't help.

