I appreciate your response, and will look up those references you
mention.

I suppose my points, which maybe I didn't make that well, were:

1) Contrary to popular opinion, this is not a country in which one
can do whatever they want.  I have been hearing people on this thread
saying "I can do what I want and no one can stop me, and conversly, 
no one can make me do anything that I don't want to do".  I was trying
to point out to those people that this is what all laws really are.
Either they are telling you that you cannot do something that you
want to do (i.e. You can't drive over 55 mph, you can't drink unless you're
21, etc.) or they are telling you that you have to do something which
you do not want to do (i.e. pay taxes, register for the draft).

Anyone who thinks that they are completely free to do what they want
is, by definition, and anarchist.

2) I used the word f*** to press my point.  I was "free" to write whatever
I wanted and if it offended anyone, that was their problem and not mine.


